{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/961084-those-who-were-meant-to-be-devoured-but-became-something-else-instead","id":961084,"title":"Those who were meant to be devoured, but became something else instead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T09:22:33-07:00","id":961084,"title":"Those who were meant to be devoured, but became something else instead","content":"I've been dwelling on an idea for character who was experiencing nightmares and on her way to becoming a Beast- but died before it could all happen. She ended up making a deal with a Geist, instead. This got me thinking about the concert in a broader sense. Supposed to be devoured, was embraced instead. Made a deal with a Geist after death. So on, and so forth. <br /> <br /> I'm wondering what everyone's interpretation would be. What kind of influence would this sort of origin have? Would it even have any lasting effects? Or would the Primordial Horror prevent something such as an embrace? Which supernatural types do you envision this being possible with, and which one's aren't plausible? <br /> <br /> <i>(Not worried about what's in the rules. I'm looking for personal head-cannon. But if there's something in the rules that I missed, please, throw a page number at me).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1948-matriarch","name":"Matriarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1948_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T09:50:27-07:00","id":961093,"title":"","content":"A Mage or Vampire could manifest a unique Legacy or Bloodline, for starters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:02:33-07:00","id":961096,"title":"","content":"Here's sort of a sideways way of looking at it. Given the family resemblance many Beasts have to the other splats and the exploratory nature of those connected to the Primordial Dream, could it not be possible that those on the cusp of becoming a Beast are actually <i>more</i> likely than your average mortal to have a brush with the supernatural and wind up a different creature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:52:34-07:00","id":961310,"title":"","content":"I'd wager if a potential Beast were to instead Awaken, they'd likely find themselves drawn to Mind even if they don't wind up as a Mastigos. Changelings likewise would probably wind up with a knack for oneiromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:16:11-07:00","id":961792,"title":"","content":"I'd wonder how the Primordial Dream would interact with someone whose nightmares attracted the attentions of one of the True Fae. Would the Horror be able to reach all the way to Faerie? Or would it need to wait until the nascent changeling struggled out to the Hedge?<br /> <br /> The fact that many of the Devoured see themselves and the Lost as being about the same thing \u2013 perhaps believing the Primordial Dream as a dark yin to the Temenos' bright yang \u2013 means that the differences between a changeling marked by the Dark Mother before her durance and a properly devoured Beast could be minimal in terms of what either 'splat' sees. That is, the Contracts of the Lost can be mistaken for Nightmares if played right, and how's a Hollow with some primordial pathways functionally different from a Lair to a Beast who really, really wants to see them as being the same? The fae mien of a changeling can resemble something from a nightmare, too. I mean, sure there ARE a tremendous number of differences, but I think that it would make for some fantastic ground to explore in a mixed chronicle with the right players.<br /> <br /> Of course, the rules sets I've seen for <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> Second Edition (e.g. how the durance ends, how seemings are chosen rather than imposed, how all notions of lost agency of a character seem to be dropped from the game... not that I'm bitter about this much) don't really make sense to me in terms of how the Lost are described in <b>Beast</b>, so take whatever I offer as a naff interpretation of a gamer who wants to see only one version of the game I so dearly love. That I'm a sceptic about this is MY deal, not yours. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:08:02-07:00","id":961948,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it is count, but I have made an hunter conspiracy which its shtick is taking the unborn Horror of a potential beast and turn it into a spirit guide/ virtual avatar (depends on the Era) to create new hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:35:22-07:00","id":962198,"title":"","content":"A Changeling who has to deal with a Horror trying to Devour them properly (now a lethal prospect, given changelings exist physically in dreams) could be interesting, and tie into a long road home in fascinating ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:54:11-07:00","id":966187,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your thoughts everyone! Good food for thought. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1948-matriarch","name":"Matriarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1948_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:10:04-07:00","id":968329,"title":"","content":"I must be the boring guy. I just ruled that the conversation to another major supernatural severs the ties to the undevoured's horror and the horror becomes a unfettered spirit roaming the primordial dream simply following it's base hunger. The undevoured would probably forever feel like something isn't right and that they are incomplete or unfulfilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}